  "payload": {
    "attribution": "William E. Salazar, Gaurav Saxena, Jack S. Baker, Leong Chuan Kwek, Thi Ha Kyaw; arXiv:2608.14798v1. Author assertion, not independent endorsement.",
    "comparison_baseline": "See source-specific comparison in the statement and conditions; no independent prior-knowledge baseline was searched.",
    "components": [
      {
        "component_id": "component:pseudomagic-mean",
        "role": "CONCLUSION",
        "source_span_refs": [
          {
            "content_hash": "sha256:b47b0727da2d208666aad06cfa46584bbea640d6e6c2c8efd9bac44c4ad8f585",
            "record_id": "example:2608.14798v1-db635458e365-span-1131-1172",
            "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
            "revision": 1
          }
        ],
        "text": "For full-support subset phase states, the authors give a closed expression for the ensemble-average stabilizer partition function and state that its curves become exponentially close to Haar curves, limiting efficient discrimination. This is an unverified author-claim candidate."
      }
    ],
    "conditions": [
      {
        "condition_id": "condition:pseudomagic-mean-0",
        "origin": "SOURCE_RECONSTRUCTED",
        "source_span_refs": [
          {
            "content_hash": "sha256:b47b0727da2d208666aad06cfa46584bbea640d6e6c2c8efd9bac44c4ad8f585",
            "record_id": "example:2608.14798v1-db635458e365-span-1131-1172",
            "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
            "revision": 1
          }
        ],
        "statement": "The subset phase state is |psi_(f,S)> = |S|^(-1/2) sum_(x in S) (-1)^f(x)|x>."
      },
      {
        "condition_id": "condition:pseudomagic-mean-1",
        "origin": "SOURCE_RECONSTRUCTED",
        "source_span_refs": [
          {
            "content_hash": "sha256:b47b0727da2d208666aad06cfa46584bbea640d6e6c2c8efd9bac44c4ad8f585",
            "record_id": "example:2608.14798v1-db635458e365-span-1131-1172",
            "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
            "revision": 1
          }
        ],
        "statement": "The theorem specializes to S={0,1}^n and |S|=2^n, with d_n=2^n."
      },
      {
        "condition_id": "condition:pseudomagic-mean-2",
        "origin": "SOURCE_RECONSTRUCTED",
        "source_span_refs": [
          {
            "content_hash": "sha256:b47b0727da2d208666aad06cfa46584bbea640d6e6c2c8efd9bac44c4ad8f585",
            "record_id": "example:2608.14798v1-db635458e365-span-1131-1172",
            "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
            "revision": 1
          }
        ],
        "statement": "The source describes f as pseudorandom and the sampling as uniform over the full-support subset phase states, without specifying the function-family distribution."
      },
      {
        "condition_id": "condition:pseudomagic-mean-3",
        "origin": "SOURCE_RECONSTRUCTED",
        "source_span_refs": [
          {
            "content_hash": "sha256:b47b0727da2d208666aad06cfa46584bbea640d6e6c2c8efd9bac44c4ad8f585",
            "record_id": "example:2608.14798v1-db635458e365-span-1131-1172",
            "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
            "revision": 1
          }
        ],
        "statement": "The theorem does not explicitly restrict beta beyond the preceding real-valued definition."
      }
    ],
